  <front>
    <title>The 'tn3270' URI Scheme</title>
    <seriesInfo name="RFC" value="6270" stream="IETF"/>
    <author fullname="M. Yevstifeyev" initials="M." surname="Yevstifeyev">
      <address>
        <postal>
          <street>8 Kuzovkov St., flat 25,</street>
          <city>Kotovsk</city>
          <country>Ukraine</country>
        </postal>
        <email>evnikita2@gmail.com</email>
      </address>
    </author>
    <date year="2011" month="June"/>
    <abstract pn="section-abstract">
      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-1">This document is the specification of the 'tn3270' Uniform Resource
Identifier (URI) scheme, which is used to designate the access to the
resources available via Telnet 3270 mode (TN3270) and Telnet 3270
Enhanced mode (TN3270E).  It updates RFC 1041 and RFC 2355, which
specify these protocols, and RFC 1738, which firstly mentioned this
URI scheme without defining its syntax and semantics.</t>
    </abstract>
